# Settings the REPOSITORY owns, pushed into the instance's env file by
# every deploy (reconcile-settings.sh, called from update.sh).
#
# WHAT BELONGS HERE: configuration that is not a secret and that should be
# the same on every instance unless somebody deliberately says otherwise.
# The model is the case that forced this file into existence — it is not a
# secret, our own docs say it belongs in version control, and yet it lived
# only in /etc/agentic-pms/api.env where no deploy was allowed to reach
# it. "Change the model and deploy" quietly did nothing, twice.
#
# WHAT MUST NEVER BE HERE: anything secret. ANTHROPIC_API_KEY,
# DATABASE_URL, JWT_SECRET and their kind stay in api.env, owned by the
# instance, untouched by deploys — that is the whole reason api.env is
# never overwritten. reconcile-settings.sh REFUSES to apply a key whose
# name looks secret rather than trusting this comment to be read.
#
# TO PIN A BOX to a different value, add to its api.env:
#     UNMANAGED=AI_MODEL
# and the deploy will leave that key alone and say so in its output.

AI_MODEL=claude-opus-5-5
